SDUSD::withdraw
├── when requested assets exceeds maxWithdraw for owner
│   └── it should revert with ERC4626ExceededMaxWithdraw
└── when requested assets does not exceed maxWithdraw for owner
    ├── when caller is neither owner nor sufficiently approved
    │   └── it should revert with ERC20InsufficientAllowance
    ├── when receiver is zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ERC20InvalidReceiver
    └── when caller is authorized
        ├── it should calculate shares to burn by rounding up
        ├── it should decrease accountedAssets by the withdrawn assets
        ├── it should decrease depositCapUsage by the DUSD withdrawn
        ├── it should burn the calculated shares from owner
        ├── it should transfer exactly the requested DUSD assets to receiver
        ├── it should return the burned share amount
        ├── it should emit Withdraw
        ├── it should not decrease the exchange rate because burned shares round up in favor of the vault
        ├── when caller is owner
        │   └── it should not require or spend an allowance
        ├── when caller is approved with a finite allowance
        │   └── it should decrease allowance by the burned shares
        ├── when caller is approved with maximum allowance
        │   └── it should leave the allowance unchanged
        ├── when requested assets is zero
        │   ├── it should complete without changing accounting, token balances, or share balances
        │   ├── it should leave depositCapUsage unchanged
        │   ├── it should leave the exchange rate unchanged
        │   └── it should emit Withdraw with zero assets and shares
        ├── when PAUSE_TYPE is paused
        │   └── it should remain available
        ├── when a reward period is active
        │   ├── it should set maxWithdraw to the owner's share of currently unlocked assets
        │   ├── it should revert above that maximum
        │   ├── it should not make locked rewards withdrawable
        │   ├── it should leave the reward amount and period boundaries unchanged
        │   ├── it should reduce cap usage by all withdrawn assets, including released rewards
        │   └── it should not decrease the remaining holders' exchange rate
        ├── when owner withdraws all available assets
        │   ├── it should leave the permanent seed shares in total supply
        │   └── without rewards it should leave only the exempt seed assets and zero cap usage
        └── when the vault has received a raw DUSD donation
            ├── it should not make the donation withdrawable
            ├── it should leave the exchange rate unchanged
            └── a subsequent withdrawal should not decrease the remaining holders' exchange rate
